WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.656
This is Coding Exercise 1 Your task is to return
patients who

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:11.764
have admissions The output needs patient ID patient
name admission ID diagnosis

00:00:11.935 --> 00:00:17.494
and department Because the question is specifically
about patients with matching

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.199
admissions think about which join requires a match
Start with patients

00:00:23.212 --> 00:00:26.712
as p and admissions as a Decide what condition
connects the two

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:33.084
tables Then select the requested fields and sort the
result Do

00:00:33.111 --> 00:00:37.640
not worry about producing one row per patient The
correct grain is

00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:41.206
one row per matching admission so patients with more
than one admission

00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:46.446
should appear more than once Write the SQL directly
in the browser

00:00:46.459 --> 00:00:50.264
and use Run and Check If your query runs but does
not

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.619
pass inspect the columns and row count rather than
randomly changing syntax

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.448
You can also copy your work into pgAdmin for
additional practice
